## =============================================================================
## INSTRUCTOR ONLY: Logistic Regression vs CART vs kNN vs RBF SVM on the
## Nonlinear Earnings-Growth Dataset
## =============================================================================
##
## PURPOSE
##   Validates the pedagogical suitability of
##   data/earnings_ratio_data_nonlinear.xlsx (generated by
##   SimulatedData-NonlinearClassification.R) by estimating, on identical
##   predictors and identical partitions:
##     1. Logistic regression, additive linear terms
##     2. Logistic regression + engineered features matching the true DGP
##        (oracle functional forms and knots; coefficients still estimated)
##     3. A single CART classification tree
##     4. k-nearest neighbors
##     5. RBF-kernel SVM
##   plus an "oracle" reference that scores firms with the true systematic
##   signal S (the Bayes-optimal ranking with complete, error-free ratios).
##
## PROTOCOL
##   - Target: Bad_Earnings = 1(Quarterly_Earnings_Growth <= Q15), derived
##     from the workbook exactly as students will. The Q15 cutoff uses the
##     full sample; it is a fixed labeling convention, not a fitted model
##     quantity, and it uses no predictor information.
##   - Predictors (identical for every method): 15 ratios + Sector.
##   - Stratified 60/20/20 train / validation / test partitions.
##   - Preprocessing -- median imputation, Sector one-hot encoding (reference
##     = first level), centering and scaling -- is fit on training rows only,
##     and re-fit inside every CV fold during tuning. Scaling is required for
##     kNN and SVM; it is harmless for logistic regression and CART.
##   - Tuning: 5-fold stratified CV within the training set, maximizing ROC
##     AUC. Ties are broken toward the simpler model.
##   - Class imbalance (common to every method): NO resampling. Balanced
##     class weighting where the method supports it (logistic case weights,
##     CART equal priors, SVM class weights; kNN ranking is invariant to
##     class-weighted voting). Every model returns a continuous risk score;
##     hyperparameters are tuned on ROC AUC (prevalence-invariant); each
##     model's classification threshold is chosen on the VALIDATION set by
##     maximizing Youden's J (sensitivity + specificity - 1). Sensitivity,
##     specificity, precision and F1 on the test set use that threshold.
##   - The test set is never used for tuning, threshold selection, or DGP
##     calibration; it is scored once per replicate.
##   - Stability: (a) repeated partitions of the course dataset (seed 2026);
##     (b) independent datasets regenerated with other simulation seeds.
##
## OUTPUTS (Topics/Classification/InstructorDiagnostics/)
##   clf_metrics_partitions.csv, clf_metrics_seeds.csv, clf_summary.csv,
##   clf_tuning.csv, clf_*.png decision-boundary figures.
##
## =============================================================================

